From c8b4db1bc191e6020bd925b8f42a236a4208a395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:52:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: built for Android libc: sound and the microphone
 through Spatiand's room

Android has no PulseAudio to play into the room's per-window sinks as the Deck does, so each
stream goes to the room's own socket, $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/spatiand-sound, under the name of its
window's sink (spatiand.window.<slot>, which SpatiandWindowAudio makes the tab's output device
from spatiand-sinks, as on the Deck); the room places it at that window through its HRTF. The
microphone is the room's too: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/spatiand-mic, recorded while a page listens.
---
